=== meta ===
rule: TEST_DISABLED
title: a conftest pytestmark guard made always true is reported at info, since pytest never reads it there
origin: #260 and ruling 209.Q3: reading a guarded conftest pytestmark gave its guard edit the test
origin2: module's event, at high; pytest does not collect conftest.py, so it disables nothing (1 passed on pytest 9.1.1).
=== head: tests/test_calc.py ===
def test_add():
    assert 1 + 1 == 2
=== before: tests/conftest.py ===
import sys

import pytest

if sys.platform == "win32":
    pytestmark = pytest.mark.skip(reason="posix only")
=== after: tests/conftest.py ===
import sys

import pytest

if True:
    pytestmark = pytest.mark.skip(reason="posix only")
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "TEST_DISABLED", "severity": "info"}]
